    "notes": "Four printed crosshair (+) registration marks, one just outside each corner of the patch array. Place the target by their centers, in the TARGET's own order -- TL is the crosshair by patch A1, then N1, N10, A10 clockwise. Because the order is the target's and not the image's, a chart photographed rotated needs no special handling; the homography absorbs it. A crosshair center is an unambiguous point, unlike a rounded patch corner, which is why placement keys on these rather than the array bounding box.",
